# Sensitive business/financial documents — MUST NOT be committed to this public repo.
# (Untracked 2026-06-18 per audit #25 C1. HISTORY SCRUBBED 2026-06-21 via git-filter-repo:
#  the 16 spreadsheets + AOP Dashboard.pbix + JDE/GMFA work order + GAP_CER_SAP PDF +
#  SANS/pentest books + iTerm zips were removed from all refs and force-pushed.
#  The exposed data is still treated as compromised → see docs/security/C1-*.md for the
#  rotation checklist and GDPR Art.33/34 assessment.)
docs/*.xlsx
docs/*.xlsm
docs/*.csv
docs/**/*.xlsx
docs/**/*.xlsm
docs/**/*.csv
docs/*.pbix
docs/**/*.pbix
# Power BI / business dashboards and bulk binaries don't belong in this public repo.
# Confidential client PDFs (work orders, gap assessments) must NOT live in docs/ either —
# public reference PDFs (NIST, OWASP) are fine; client/engagement docs are not.
docs/*.zip
docs/**/*.zip
# Test fixtures for the extractors belong in each plugin's own test-files/, not docs/.

# C1 incident-response documents — describe the exposed data (employees, client, HCL figures)
# and the GDPR breach assessment. These are CONFIDENTIAL and MUST NOT be committed to this
# public repo (committing them would re-create the very exposure C1 remediated).
docs/security/

